WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.440 line:87%
If I had the power to change something
for young people in Europe,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.120 line:87%
I would tell them that they have the right
of co-decision on policy.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.720 line:87%
At school we were taught to just follow
the rules, but that's not true.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.360 line:87%
We can co-decide on the rules and in
that way make a better youth policy.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.480 line:87%
Structured Dialogue
is an initiative of Europe.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.320 line:87%
It connects young people and
policymakers in a structured way

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.360 line:94%
in order to draw up policy proposals.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.160 line:87%
During the conference
I got to meet a policymaker.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.720 line:94%
We exchanged some ideas.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.680 line:87%
He was very interested
in what I had to say,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.480 line:87%
what I had learned,
what I was involved in.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.280 line:87%
He stood much closer to the youth
than I had imagined.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.080 line:87%
That was a very interesting discussion
I had with Ines

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.960 line:87%
because clearly she comes
from a very participatory background.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.720 line:87%
She's a chairwoman
of a local youth council

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.800 line:87%
and I was quite impressed
because she's very well informed

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.560 line:87%
about the way participation
happens at local level,

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.480 line:87%
what are the challenges,
what are the solutions.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.160 line:87%
Also she's taking part
in this European policy process.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.000 line:87%
Meeting people was one goal of this
conference. That was accomplished.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.560 line:87%
I met a lot of people
from many countries.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.960 line:94%
Many nice, young, committed people.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.800 line:87%
In spite of our different languages,
the communication went very well.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.960 line:87%
I think that through engaging in
discussions with policymakers,

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.480 line:94%
both learn.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.240 line:87%
I think that policymakers, they learn
more of the reality of young people

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.400 line:87%
and young people also they can maybe
have a more complex view

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.760 line:94%
on how policymaking works.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.880 line:94%
One example that illustrates quite well

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.440 line:87%
how policymaking
or Structured Dialogue works

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.240 line:94%
is the Youth Guarantee.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.360 line:87%
The current scheme of the Youth
Guarantee that is being implemented

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.680 line:87%
in almost all the Member States
is something that appeared also

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.320 line:87%
in the Structured Dialogue’s national
consultations and youth conferences.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.920 line:87%
So this is something I can say
that can be traced back among others

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.640 line:94%
to the Structured Dialogue.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.280 line:87%
It looks very complicated, but
it's much more accessible than it seems.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.840 line:87%
This is a new opportunity to learn
new things, to get more chances.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.120 line:94%
To build a brighter future for ourselves.

